  "landfallEstimate": "Movement towards Andhra Pradesh &",
  "rawBulletin": "India Meteorological Department\n(Ministry of Earth Sciences)\nNATIONAL BULLETIN NO. 8 (BOB/10/2026)\nTIME OF ISSUE:1600 HOURS IST DATED:16.11.2026\nFROM: INDIA METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT (FAX NO. 24643965/24699216/24623220)\nTO: CONTROL ROOM, NDM, MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS (FAX.NO. 23093750)\nCONTROL ROOM NDMA (FAX.NO. 26701729)\nCABINET SECRETARIAT (FAX.NO.23012284, 23018638)\nPS TO HON\u2019BLE MINISTER FOR S & T AND EARTH SCIENCES (FAX NO.23316745)\nSECRETARY, MOES (FAX NO. 24629777)\nH.Q. (INTEGRATED DEFENCE STAFF AND CDS) (FAX NO. 23005137/23005147)\nDIRECTOR GENERAL, DOORDARSHAN (23385843)\nDIRECTOR GENERAL, AIR (23421105, 23421219)\nPIB MOES (FAX NO. 23389042)\nUNI (FAX NO. 23355841)\nD.G. NATIONAL DISASTER RESPONSE FORCE (NDRF) (FAX NO. 26105912, 2436 3260)\nDIRECTOR, PUNCTUALITY, INDIAN RAILWAYS (FAX NO. 23388503)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF ANDAMAN & NICOBAR ISLANDS (FAX NO. 03192-232656)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF ANDHRA PRADESH (FAX NO. 0863-2441029)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF ODISHA (FAX NO. 0674-2536660)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT OF TELANGANA (FAX NO 040-23455340)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF TAMIL NADU (FAX NO. 044-25672304)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF PUDUCHERRY (FAX NO. 0413-2334145)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF CHHATTISGARH (FAX NO. 0771-2221206)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF JHARKHAND (FAX NO. 0651-2400255)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF WEST BENGAL (FAX NO. 033-22144328)\nSub: Deep Depression over Southeast & adjoining Southwest Bay of Bengal [Pre Cyclone Watch\nfor Andhra Pradesh & adjoining South Odisha coast Yellow Message]\nThe Deep Depression over Southeast & adjoining Southwest Bay of Bengal moved north-northwestwards\nwith the speed of 17 kmph during past 06 hours and lay centered at 1130 hours IST of today, the 16th\nNovember, 2026 over the same region, near Latitude 11.7\u00b0N and Longitude 86.0\u00b0E, about 620 km\nnortheast of Trincomalee (Sri Lanka), 730km west of Sri Vijaya Puram (Andaman & Nicobar Islands), 650\nkm east-southeast of Chennai (Tamil Nadu), 730 km south-southeast of Visakhapatnam (Andhra\nPradesh) and 850 km south of Gopalpur (Odisha).\nIt is very likely to continue to move north-northwestwards, intensify further into a Cyclonic Storm over the\ncentral parts of south & adjoining westcentral Bay of Bengal in the evening of today, the 16th November\nand into a Severe Cyclonic Storm over westcentral Bay of Bengal in the evening of 17th November, 2026.\nThereafter, it is likely to intensify further and move west-northwestwards and cross Andhra Pradesh &\nYanam coasts between Nellore and Tuni, around noon of 20th November, 2026 as a very severe cyclonic\nstorm with the maximum sustained wind speed of 120-130 kmph gusting to 145 kmph.\nForecast location and intensity are given in following table:\nDate/Time Position Maximum sustained surface Category of cyclonic\n(IST) (Lat. 0N/ long. 0E) wind speed (Kmph) disturbance\n16.11.26/1130 11.7/86.0 50-60 gusting to 70 Deep Depression\n16.11.26/1730 12.2/85.7 60-70 gusting to 80 Cyclonic Storm\n16.11.26/2330 12.6/85.4 70-80 gusting to 90 Cyclonic Storm\n17.11.26/0530 13.0/84.9 80-90 gusting to 100 Cyclonic Storm\n17.11.26/1130 13.4/84.3 90-100 gusting to 110 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n17.11.26/2330 13.8/83.7 95-105 gusting to 115 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n18.11.26/1130 14.2/83.2 100-110 gusting to 120 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n18.11.26/2330 14.7/82.6 105-115 gusting to 125 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n19.11.26/1130 15.1/82.1 105-115 gusting to 125 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n19.11.26/2330 15.4/81.6 115-125 gusting to 140 Very Severe Cyclonic Storm\n20.11.26/1130 15.8/81.0 120-130 gusting to 145 Very Severe Cyclonic Storm\n20.11.26/2330 16.2/79.9 90-100 gusting to 110 Severe Cyclonic Storm\nWarnings:\n(i) Rainfall Warning:\nTamil Nadu, Puducherry & Karaikal: Light to moderate rainfall at many places with heavy rainfall at\nisolated places is very likely over North Tamil Nadu, Puducherry & Karaikal on 17th & 20th with heavy to\nvery heavy rainfall at isolated places on 18th & 19th November.\nCoastal Andhra Pradesh: Light to moderate rainfall at many pla",
